                    insight_win:            `Institutional entrepreneur: you moved the regulatory outcome by working with the consumer-protection logic rather than against it. You secured amendments to the cap, raised your legitimacy with the CRE, held coalition strength and defended the €180M fair-price brand — all four KPIs at once.`,
                    insight_pyrrhic:        `A Pyrrhic win: you softened the cap, but the aggressive campaign or a toxic coalition cost you the brand. You protected €124M of margin and spent €180M of reputation — the trust crisis outweighs the regulatory gain.`,
                    insight_escalated:      `You triggered the statute: an obstructive, self-interested campaign convinced the Ministry to bypass the CRE and legislate directly — a harsher, non-negotiable rule. Fighting the whole draft or free-riding the association forfeited the negotiable outcome.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short on the regulatory outcome. The cap stands largely as drafted, and the margin compression bites. Re-examine your stance, your frame and which amendments you actually pursued.`,
                    insight_brand:          `Your reputation dropped below the line where the fair-price premium holds. The brand was your most valuable non-market asset — engagement that spends it can cost more than the regulation it was meant to fix.`,
